        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Financial Accounting",
        "topic": "Financial Ratios",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2004",
        "question_text": "<p>The formula for calculating the <b>current ratio</b> is:</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The <b>current ratio</b> measures liquidity and is calculated as:<br><b>Current Ratio = Current Assets / Current Liabilities</b>.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "61372",
